# Equal Protection and Due Process: Contrasting Methods of Review under Fourteenth Amendment Doctrine.

**Authors:** Hughes, James A.

## Abstract
Argues that the Court has, at times, confused equal protection and due process methods of review, primarily by employing interest balancing in certain equal protection cases that should have been subjected to due process analysis. Available from Harvard Civil Rights-Civil Liberties Law Review, Harvard Law School, Cambridge, MA 02138; sc $4.00. (Author/IRT)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ214260

